"""Fabloom: network configs generated by a model, verified by Batfish, repaired until they pass.

Planes and their boundary rules (enforced by ``.importlinter``, ADR-0001):

- ``contracts``  Pydantic models. Zero I/O. Imports nothing else in fabloom.
- ``checks``     Deterministic intent -> check-set compiler. Depends only on ``contracts``.
- ``verify``     Verifier protocol and backends. Never imports ``llm`` or ``agent``.
- ``llm``        Token Factory client, model routing, cost accounting, prompts.
- ``agent``      The run state machine: planner -> generator -> verifier -> repairer -> explainer.
- ``scrub``      Secret redaction on the ingress and logging paths.

The rule that makes the project credible: the model cannot influence what it is graded on.
"""

from importlib.metadata import PackageNotFoundError, version

try:
    __version__ = version("fabloom")
except PackageNotFoundError:  # pragma: no cover - only when running from an uninstalled tree
    __version__ = "0.0.0+unknown"

__all__ = ["__version__"]
